{
  "$comment": "Prompt enhancement (interaction spec 3.7). One set of rules for the Server (managed jobs: CompleteInternal on a managed text model, not billed, no free-quota use) and the three clients (BYOK / relay: the client calls a chat model itself). scripts/studio-contracts-check.mjs recomputes every case with scripts/lib/studio-prompt-enhance-reference.mjs. adds estimate (BYOK / relay price line) and outcome (what a round records from the result); the check recomputes both.",
  "contractId": "studio_prompt_enhance",
  "version": 1,
  "constants": {
    "timeoutMs": 15000,
    "maxOutputTokens": 1024,
    "maxPromptCodePoints": 32000,
    "titleMaxCodePoints": 200,
    "workTitleGraphemes": 12,
    "quotePairs": [
      [
        "\"",
        "\""
      ],
      [
        "“",
        "”"
      ],
      [
        "「",
        "」"
      ],
      [
        "『",
        "』"
      ]
    ]
  },
  "rules": {
    "request": "System prompt = instruction (verbatim), one user message = userMessage(operation, prompt) where prompt is the composed prompt (studio_prompt_compose: user text + Style / Effects lines). Reasoning suppressed, maxOutputTokens, one attempt, whole call bounded by timeoutMs. Timeout, transport or upstream error, or a parse failure -> the image request uses the composed prompt unchanged and the result is failed.",
    "parse": "Take the reply from its first \"{\" to its last \"}\" and parse it as JSON (anything else, or no braces -> invalid_output); it must be an object whose prompt is a string (else invalid_output). prompt is trimmed (Unicode White_Space only; U+FEFF is not whitespace, so JS String.trim / \\s must not be used); empty -> empty_prompt; contains a lone surrogate (from a JSON escape) or U+FFFD -> invalid_output; more than maxPromptCodePoints code points (case maxPromptCodePoints overrides the constant) -> too_long. Every quoted segment of the original prompt must appear verbatim (substring, case-sensitive) in the new prompt, else quote_changed; the quote marks themselves may change.",
    "quotedSegments": "Scan the original left to right; at an opener of quotePairs find the next matching closer; found -> its contents (between the marks) are one segment, scanning resumes after the closer, so quotes nested inside a segment are covered by it; no closer -> the opener is plain text. Segments whose contents are only whitespace are skipped. Single quotes are never quote marks (apostrophes).",
    "title": "title: not a string -> null; trim, collapse every run of Unicode White_Space to one space, strip quote marks (\" ' “ ” ‘ ’ 「 」 『 』) at both ends, trim again; empty, more than titleMaxCodePoints code points, or containing a lone surrogate or U+FFFD -> null. The parse result keeps the full title; the work name is workTitle = first workTitleGraphemes grapheme clusters with trailing whitespace dropped, and the first-sentence rule when title is null or enhancement failed.",
    "managedSubmit": "Managed submit body: enhance: true only when the switch is on (omitted otherwise, same idempotency hash as before); style / effect fragments travel inside prompt as today (no separate fields); advanced fields stay out of the managed body. Compare submissions are separate jobs and each is enhanced on its own (its round card shows its own sent text), the same per-job rule as BYOK where each connection uses its own chat model.",
    "jobView": "Job view (GET / list / cancel) and the job.completed event carry optional prompt_enhance only when the job asked for it: {status: pending|applied|failed, prompt, title}; pending until the executor has run it (the Server reports a terminal job still pending as failed, e.g. cancelled or failed before enhancement ran), prompt (the text actually sent) and title (omitted when null) only with applied. Client decode: missing, null, not an object, unknown status, applied without a non-empty string prompt -> null; prompt / title read only for applied (title not a non-empty string -> null). When the prompt retention expires the Server clears the enhanced prompt and title with the job prompt: status stays, prompt / title are omitted, so clients decode an expired applied as null.",
    "estimate": "Price line (BYOK / relay only; managed enhancement is not billed, no line): shown when funding is byok or relay, the switch is on (toggle on) and the chat model price is known; it is not added to the total. inputTokens = ceil(UTF-8 bytes of instruction + \"\\n\" + userMessage(operation, composed prompt) / 4); outputTokens = maxOutputTokens; prices are integer micro-USD per 1M tokens (catalog USD per 1M tokens x 10^6, rounded); per call micro-USD = ceil((inputTokens x input + outputTokens x output) / 10^6) with integer math; microUsd = per call x jobs (byok / relay jobs in the submission, each enhanced on its own). Missing / negative / non-integer price or jobs < 1 -> null (line hidden, never shown as 0 or as unavailable).",
    "outcome": "What a round records once its enhancement result is known (BYOK / relay: parse result; managed: decoded prompt_enhance). Not requested -> nothing, whatever the result. applied -> enhancedPrompt = the sent prompt; failed -> notApplied (round card shows the not-applied mark, the composed prompt was sent); pending or null (not run yet, or expired) -> nothing. workTitle: only for a work created by this submission whose title is still empty, from the first applied result with a non-null title -> workTitle(title); otherwise null (the first-sentence fallback stays)."
  },
  "instruction": "You rewrite prompts for an image generation model.\nRewrite the user prompt into one complete, vivid English description, keeping every style and effect note it contains.\nIf the operation is edit, the prompt is an instruction to change a provided image: keep it an instruction, made clearer and more specific, instead of describing a new image.\nKeep every piece of text inside quotation marks (\"...\", “...”, 「...」, 『...』) exactly as written, in its original language; do not translate it.\nDo not add text that should appear in the image unless the user asked for it.\nAlso write a short title for the artwork in the language of the user prompt, at most 12 characters.\nReply with JSON only: {\"prompt\": \"...\", \"title\": \"...\"}",
  "userMessage": [
    {
      "name": "generate",
      "operation": "generate",
      "prompt": "a cat\nStyle: watercolor.",
      "expect": "Operation: generate\nPrompt:\na cat\nStyle: watercolor."
    },
    {
      "name": "edit",
      "operation": "edit",
      "prompt": "Make the sky blue",
      "expect": "Operation: edit\nPrompt:\nMake the sky blue"
    }
  ],
